<title>GERMANY: Eurostat says EU gold sale rules apply to all.</title>
<headline>Eurostat says EU gold sale rules apply to all.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The acting director of Eurostat, Daniel Byk, said on Thursday that European Union (EU) rules stating that a nation cannot reduce its deficit through central bank gold sales applied to all EU nations.</p>
<p>&quot;The rules apply to all countries,&quot; Byk Told Reuters in response to a question on whether Germany's government could legitimately sell Bundesbank gold to help reduce its budget deficit.</p>
<p>EU rules state that gold sales from central banks can be used only to reduce the government debt, but not to cut the deficit.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt newsroom +49 69 7565 1246</p>
</text>
